{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15673-how-would-you-reflect-an-exile-mechanically","id":15673,"title":"How would you reflect an Exile, mechanically?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T15:26:49-08:00","id":15673,"title":"How would you reflect an Exile, mechanically?","content":"Exiles are one of my favorite unexpected surprises of Descent, and one of my characters may end up eventually becoming one.<br /> <br /> How would you show them mechanically? I can't think of how to differentiate them from Angels or Demons, or even if they need to be different. H-E-L-P!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:38:09-08:00","id":15682,"title":"","content":"Well one thing we know about them is can be ageless. And due to their nature they should have no problem Going Loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T09:30:57-08:00","id":16135,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, they feel like they should work much like angels, but without the sense of purpose - my impression was that they're basically angels without Orders To Be Getting On With.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T09:49:14-08:00","id":16145,"title":"","content":"Some are Angels, but others are Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:23:34-08:00","id":16165,"title":"","content":"You -could- portray one with a demon's sheet. Give him some numina, maybe disregard cover...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:29:46-08:00","id":17084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15673-how-would-you-reflect-an-exile-mechanically?p=16145#post16145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some are Angels, but others are Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the ones who were Demons were when the G-M picks them up for recycling - so they've been returned to angelhood, but imperfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:41:42-08:00","id":17091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15673-how-would-you-reflect-an-exile-mechanically?p=17084#post17084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the ones who were Demons were when the G-M picks them up for recycling - so they've been returned to angelhood, but imperfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope they are Exiles. If the Godmachine can recycle unwilling Demons why would a willing demon somehow cause a bug? Exiles are Angels who didn't Fall the way and are kind of stuck mid fall, and Demons who the Godmachine reconnected rather recycled. They are explicitly said to be ageless too. The imperfection is that they are not made Angels again, they are still material demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:36:37-08:00","id":21973,"title":"","content":"To me most important is to roleplay them correctly. just cheat the rules when it suits. think matrix reloaded, the architect, the oracle, the merovingian, the keymaker, etc. they have no motives... they go on about their &quot;function.&quot; i'd say the merovingian is on the verge of a Fall though. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1475-scorpionx1","name":"scorpionx1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T13:38:57-08:00","id":23942,"title":"","content":"A lot of mechanics can be hand-waved or cheated by the Storyteller end if they'll only apply to NPCs. If a PC Integrator wants to become an exile, however, you have a few mechanical dials depending on the circumstances of their re-integration and your overall concept of how exiles work.<br /> <br /> Some possible advantages:<ul><li>An exile would face reduced risk from compromise rolls. This is the main advantage, and could mean any or all of the following:<ul><li>An exile won't be hunted no matter how low their Cover drops, but still needs to maintain their Cover(s) if they want to pass as mortal.</li> <li>At least one of their Covers has a fixed rating that never drops below $VALUE, and/or they can't get rid of it. They may or may not be able to acquire or improve new Covers, and may or may not lose the ability to Go Loud.</li> <li>An exile could have reliable (G-M sponsored) access to Cover and/or Glitch-repairing Infrastructure. This may or may not repair permanent Glitches due to a high Primum rating.</li> <li>An exile may be able to ignore compromise rolls under some, most, or all circumstances. Alternatively, an exile may treat the result of a compromise roll as the next highest result (dramatic failures are either impossible or treated like normal failures, normal failures are treated like successes, successes are treated like exceptional successes).</li> </ul></li> <li>An exile would have reliable access to Infrastructure (and Aether), again without fear of G-M harassment.</li> <li>Depending on the Storyteller (and G-M), an exile could learn Numina and/or Influences.</li> </ul>Some possible disadvantages:<ul><li>The G-M would always know where an exile is. This may extend to a permanent Condition like Surveilled or Plugged-In.</li> <li>An exile cannot Spoof the G-M or the G-M's agents; they will always detect as either an exile, an angel, or a demon (depending on how merciful the Storyteller or G-M is feeling in the circumstances).</li> <li>An exile may have more restricted options for personal advancement. This could mean any or all of the following, depending on how restrictiveness of the Storyteller and/or G-M:<ul><li>A demon turned exile may be unable to advance their Cipher as it reflects a metaphysical distinction from the G-M. They may or may not lose their Interlocks, or using them may require a compromise roll. Thought: could G-M install a replacement Cipher-like construct?</li> <li>An exile may be unable to raise their Primum for a similar reason, at least without the G-M's permission. Doing so may or may not require a compromise roll. They may or may not gain the consolation of angelic Rank.</li> <li>An exile could lose access to their Exploits, or lose the ability to learn new ones. Alternatively, learning or using new exploits could require a penalized compromise roll. An exile could face a similar issue with Embeds not associated with their Incarnation.</li> <li>*Alternatively, an exile could still access any of the above, but they'd risk Falling again.</li> </ul></li> <li>An exile may lose the ability to Go Loud, depending on the status of their Cover.</li> <li>An exile may or may not lose the ability to change or improve their Cover without G-M permission. Doing so may or may not require a compromise roll.</li> <li>An exile may or may not lose the ability to make Pacts without G-M permission. Doing so may or may not require a compromise roll.</li> </ul>Also, as mentioned in the text, some angels and most demons aren't that fond of exiles, even if they aren't automatically hostile.<br /> <br /> Exile status may be revoked by either the G-M or the ex-demon.<br /> <br /> Some of these advantages are more permissive than I'd use. I think I'd still require compromise rolls to avoid degrading Cover, but I'd give the exile relatively safe access to glitch-curing Infrastructure and/or less fear from the Hunted condition (but I'd make them keep the Glitches from high Primum). Similarly, I'm iffy on allowing access to Numina or Influences except in special circumstances.<br /> <br /> Likewise, some of these disadvantages are more restrictive than I'd use. While I'd forbid a demon-turned-exile from advancing their Cipher without risking another Fall, they'd still be able to raise Primum using XP, learn Exploits, and Go Loud (though Going Loud may still piss off the G-M).<br /> <br /> Again, some of this could depend on how the PC gained exile status. I could imagine there being different types of exile status, some more fragile or restrictive than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":".  clarification 12-05-2013, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:32:55-08:00","id":24369,"title":"","content":"I would just go the simple route of building them as the sample Exile in the book; meaning, as an Angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:12:39-08:00","id":24590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15673-how-would-you-reflect-an-exile-mechanically?p=24369#post24369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just go the simple route of building them as the sample Exile in the book; meaning, as an Angel.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, sure, but where's the fun in that? ; - ) More seriously, I got the impression somewhere along the line that demons-turned-exile were metaphysically distinct from angels-turned-exile. A demon who reconnects with the God-Machine wouldn't automatically get their ephemeral form back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:36:29-08:00","id":24606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gapb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15673-how-would-you-reflect-an-exile-mechanically?p=24590#post24590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, sure, but where's the fun in that? ; - ) More seriously, I got the impression somewhere along the line that demons-turned-exile were metaphysically distinct from angels-turned-exile. A demon who reconnects with the God-Machine wouldn't automatically get their ephemeral form back.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would rather make ex-demon exiles less effective than demons or angels.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A handful of exiles are demons who returned to the service of the God-Machine. While it almost always recycles the Unchained who turn themselves over to it, the God-Machine sends a few back into the world with their free will intact. <b>They lose some of the capabilities they gain as Unchained.</b> They otherwise suffer the same fates as other exiles \u2014 meaningless or inadequate instructions, warped or broken bodies and minds. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T21:09:25-08:00","id":24881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15673-how-would-you-reflect-an-exile-mechanically?p=24606#post24606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would rather make ex-demon exiles less effective than demons or angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I don't think that would be appropriate for the type of game I'd run. I still like the idea of an ex-demon becoming unable to progress further in their Cipher. While I'm leery about letting them do away with compromise rolls entirely, perhaps getting rid of them for Embeds, Exploits, and Demonic Form powers would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> What do you suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":". 12-07-2013, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:31:39-08:00","id":25479,"title":"","content":"If you put a gun to my head and made me run Exiles tonight, I'd run them all as angels. Yes, even demons who reconnected to the God-Machine. They have been taken to a Facility for reprocessing, leaving them in a form more trackable, predictable, and ready for communication and reintegration if the God-Machine so wishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T22:36:15-08:00","id":25610,"title":"","content":"Kirby: Right now, that's how I'd run them too. That's just what feels right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1009-kristastic","name":"Kristastic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1009_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T02:08:44-08:00","id":25690,"title":"","content":"I should point out I've also been trying to brainstorm a Manifestation for angels that give them a longer lasting corporeal form for both &quot;deep cover&quot; loyalists who are expected to deal with corporeal matters away from Infrastructure for a long time as well as for Exiles who stay mostly corporeal themselves, but I'm having no luck coming up with something interesting and flawed enough for it to be distinct from and not strictly better than normal Materialization, maintaining the sheer trauma and fundamental change of state that the Fall brings, and without obviating the need for human (or more precisely naturally corporeal) servants.<br /> <br /> Even without such a Manifestation, I'd still probably have even the most materialistic Exile be an angel, it's just very careful about the Infrastructure that hosts it and uses it as a launch point into the material world constantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 12-08-2013, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}